From 1938b937baf2a119ec275837132bfc3dc54390a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:04:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: `:focus-within` matches the focused element's
 chain (backport of #1226)

This is upstream's 38ca4e77, "Support the :focus-within pseudo-class
(#1226)" by Nico Burns and Dietmar Maurer, on 674d7d21. Its tests go in
their own files, as tests/blitz-tests has them on that base (no all.rs),
and focus_redraw.rs names Tab as that base's keyboard-types does.

Selector matching for :focus-within was stubbed to false and no element
state was kept for it. ElementState::FOCUS_WITHIN is now kept on the
focused element and its DOM ancestors, with the ancestor-path diffing
hover uses, through state snapshots: when focus moves or is cleared,
when the focused node is removed, and when a subtree that contains it
moves. A node that is not in the document is not focused. A focus change
asks for a frame where it is made, so Tab's own request goes.
